1
00:00:01,484 --> 00:00:04,694
-♪ In the not-too-distant
future ♪

2
00:00:04,728 --> 00:00:07,662
♪ Way down in Deep 13

3
00:00:07,697 --> 00:00:11,011
♪ The evil Dr. Forrester

4
00:00:11,045 --> 00:00:14,152
♪ Was hatching
a nasty scheme ♪

5
00:00:14,186 --> 00:00:16,947
♪ He hired a temp
by the name of Mike ♪

6
00:00:16,982 --> 00:00:20,192
♪ Just a regular Joe
he didn't like ♪

7
00:00:20,227 --> 00:00:23,885
♪ His experiment needed
a good test case ♪

8
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:24,990
♪ So he conked him
on the noggin ♪

9
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:26,888
♪ And he shot him into space

10
00:00:26,923 --> 00:00:29,443
-Here we go!

11
00:00:29,477 --> 00:00:32,929
-♪ I'll send him cheesy movies

12
00:00:32,963 --> 00:00:35,725
♪ The worst I can find 
-♪ La, la, la

13
00:00:35,759 --> 00:00:38,624
-♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

14
00:00:38,659 --> 00:00:41,903
♪ And I'll monitor his mind

15
00:00:41,938 --> 00:00:45,148
♪ Now, keep in mind,
Mike can't control ♪

16
00:00:45,183 --> 00:00:48,324
♪ When the movies
begin or end ♪

17
00:00:48,358 --> 00:00:51,189
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity

18
00:00:51,223 --> 00:00:54,744
♪ With the help
of his robot friends ♪

19
00:00:56,263 --> 00:00:57,885
-Robot roll call.

20
00:00:57,919 --> 00:00:59,335
Cambot.

21
00:00:59,369 --> 00:01:00,543
Gypsy.

22
00:01:00,577 --> 00:01:02,200
Tom Servo.
-Hello, there.

23
00:01:02,234 --> 00:01:03,649
-Cro-o-o-o-w.

24
00:01:03,684 --> 00:01:06,963
-♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

25
00:01:06,997 --> 00:01:09,966
♪ And other science facts 
-♪ La, la, la

26
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,107
-♪ Just repeat to yourself,
"It's just a show" ♪

27
00:01:13,142 --> 00:01:16,421
♪ "I should really
just relax" ♪

28
00:01:16,455 --> 00:01:19,113
-Did I tell you
my mother is here?

29
00:01:19,148 --> 00:01:24,705
-♪ For "Mystery Science
Theater 3000" ♪

30
00:01:26,879 --> 00:01:28,571
[Clang! Squeak! ]

31
00:01:28,605 --> 00:01:30,538
[Beeping]

32
00:01:30,573 --> 00:01:33,472
[Whirring]

33
00:01:33,507 --> 00:01:34,749
[Slam!]

34
00:01:34,784 --> 00:01:37,269
[Squeak!]

35
00:01:37,304 --> 00:01:38,857
-[Muffled screaming]

36
00:01:38,891 --> 00:01:41,549
-Hello, there.
Welcome to the SOL,

37
00:01:41,584 --> 00:01:45,139
the Satellite of Laughs,
as we like to call it.

38
00:01:45,174 --> 00:01:48,453
-We've tied up Mike and jammed
an oily rag into his mouth

39
00:01:48,487 --> 00:01:51,145
so that we may bring you
the following joke.

40
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:53,630
-You see? If you live long
enough, eventually,

41
00:01:53,665 --> 00:01:56,599
someone is going to say the word"Thunderdome" in your presence.

42
00:01:56,633 --> 00:01:58,256
-That's right, and I'm guessing
most of you

43
00:01:58,290 --> 00:02:00,189
aren't equipped
with a snappy comeback.

44
00:02:00,223 --> 00:02:02,777
Well, we're gonna
give you one.

45
00:02:02,812 --> 00:02:05,125
-We'll act it out for you.

46
00:02:05,159 --> 00:02:08,024
Boy, I still think
we really screwed up on

47
00:02:08,058 --> 00:02:10,130
that whole Thunderdome fiasco.

48
00:02:10,164 --> 00:02:14,168
-Oh, come on. Can't we just get
beyond Thunderdome?

49
00:02:14,203 --> 00:02:15,307
-[Grunting]

50
00:02:15,342 --> 00:02:16,791
-Thank you.
-Thank you. Thank you.

51
00:02:16,826 --> 00:02:18,172
Now, as you can see,

52
00:02:18,207 --> 00:02:20,726
your stooge can't mention
the movie "Beyond Thunderdome"

53
00:02:20,761 --> 00:02:22,211
because that just ruins
the whole joke.

54
00:02:22,245 --> 00:02:25,490
You'll just have to wait until
someone mentions a Thunderdome,

55
00:02:25,524 --> 00:02:28,044
not the specific one
in "Beyond Thunderdome."

56
00:02:28,078 --> 00:02:30,529
-I'm sorry, so sorry.
-Also, it really helps

57
00:02:30,564 --> 00:02:32,842
if your stooge speaks
of a Thunderdome

58
00:02:32,876 --> 00:02:35,776
in a disparaging manner,
as in our little playlet.

59
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:38,606
It'll still work if he speaks
of a Thunderdome

60
00:02:38,641 --> 00:02:41,091
in a positive light,
but if I were you,

61
00:02:41,126 --> 00:02:43,818
I'd wait until somebody
slams a Thunderdome.

62
00:02:43,853 --> 00:02:46,373
-Now, let's move on
to the rangoon version

63
00:02:46,407 --> 00:02:47,684
of this classic joke.

64
00:02:47,719 --> 00:02:48,651
-Ah, yes.
-[Grunts]

65
00:02:48,685 --> 00:02:53,759
♪♪

66
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,555
-[Laughing]

67
00:02:56,590 --> 00:02:58,695
-Yeah, real funny.
You guys finished yet?

68
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:00,076
-Oh, sure.
-Yeah, why?

69
00:03:00,110 --> 00:03:02,527
-Well, usually your little
riffs tend to go on and on,

70
00:03:02,561 --> 00:03:03,873
maybe a little...

71
00:03:03,907 --> 00:03:06,220
-Oh, please, Mike,
can't we get beyond the riff?

72
00:03:06,255 --> 00:03:08,981
-Oh! That's it.
Go to your room, both of you.

73
00:03:09,016 --> 00:03:10,776
-Huh?
-Hey, who hit that?

74
00:03:10,811 --> 00:03:11,708
-Hey.
-What's going on?

75
00:03:11,743 --> 00:03:12,847
-What?

76
00:03:12,882 --> 00:03:15,229
Oh, are you still there?
Oh, that's right.

77
00:03:15,264 --> 00:03:17,887
I forgot to disconnect
the Umbilicus.

78
00:03:17,921 --> 00:03:18,922
Look out, Mother.

79
00:03:18,957 --> 00:03:20,717
[Indistinct conversations]

80
00:03:20,752 --> 00:03:22,271
-Huh?
-Cut the Umb-- Why?

81
00:03:22,305 --> 00:03:24,376
-You can't disconnect
the Umbilicus.

82
00:03:24,411 --> 00:03:25,653
-We'll die.

83
00:03:25,688 --> 00:03:26,999
-Oh, nonsense.

84
00:03:27,034 --> 00:03:29,761
You'll be pulled into
Earth's gravitational field.

85
00:03:29,795 --> 00:03:32,488
Your orbit will decay.
The hull will rupture.

86
00:03:32,522 --> 00:03:35,215
You'll burn to a crisp,
and then you'll die.

87
00:03:38,183 --> 00:03:39,702
-What?
You -- you can't do that.

88
00:03:39,736 --> 00:03:41,566
We've done everything
you've ever asked.

89
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:43,568
We watched every bad movie
you sent up here.

90
00:03:43,602 --> 00:03:44,707
-Yeah.

91
00:03:44,741 --> 00:03:46,881
-Sorry. Bye-bye.

92
00:03:46,916 --> 00:03:49,919
-You said you'd let us
get back to Earth.

93
00:03:49,953 --> 00:03:51,265
-Did I say that?

94
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,267
Hmm.
Well, maybe I did.

95
00:03:53,302 --> 00:03:55,511
What do you want?
I'm evil.

96
00:03:55,545 --> 00:03:58,307
-Well, this is kind of sudden.

97
00:03:58,341 --> 00:03:59,963
-Look, I'm really very sorry.

98
00:03:59,998 --> 00:04:02,345
My hands are tied.
I got a letter today.

99
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:03,760
My funding has been cut,

100
00:04:03,795 --> 00:04:06,625
and you guys just aren't
cutting the mustard, so...

101
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:08,903
-Well, I'm gonna make
another trip over.

102
00:04:08,938 --> 00:04:10,180
I think I found Frank.

103
00:04:10,215 --> 00:04:12,942
-Oh, no, Mother.
That's Frank's spare head.

104
00:04:12,976 --> 00:04:15,462
Why don't we just
put that in storage?

105
00:04:15,496 --> 00:04:16,877
-Got it.
-[Sighs]

106
00:04:16,911 --> 00:04:20,294
-I'm moving back in with Mom
to save some scratch.

107
00:04:20,329 --> 00:04:22,779
At least her building
has a pool.

108
00:04:22,814 --> 00:04:24,194
I'm sorry.
What was the problem?

109
00:04:24,229 --> 00:04:27,784
-How can you do this to us?
-Ah, criminy, I got an idea.

110
00:04:27,819 --> 00:04:30,097
-What are we supposed
to do now?

111
00:04:30,131 --> 00:04:32,444
-I don't know.
Do what you always do!

112
00:04:32,479 --> 00:04:35,827
Look, I've got to fill out
these change-of-address cards.

113
00:04:35,861 --> 00:04:38,347
-Well, I'm gonna take
another load over.

114
00:04:38,381 --> 00:04:39,658
Back in a few.

115
00:04:39,693 --> 00:04:43,766
Boy, I'm glad I never
got rid of the big rig.

116
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:47,217
-Anyway, guys, your orbit will
begin to decay

117
00:04:47,252 --> 00:04:48,495
in about two hours,

118
00:04:48,529 --> 00:04:51,843
so I've downloaded a filmfrom the ship's internal memory.

119
00:04:51,877 --> 00:04:54,466
It's called "Laserblast,"

120
00:04:54,501 --> 00:04:56,848
and Leonard Maltin
gives it 2 1/2 stars.

121
00:04:56,882 --> 00:04:57,987
[Whirring]

122
00:04:58,021 --> 00:04:59,160
-Now what?

123
00:04:59,195 --> 00:05:00,886
-Thruster engines firing.

124
00:05:00,921 --> 00:05:02,578
We now have impulse power.

125
00:05:02,612 --> 00:05:05,615
-Well, how did you do that?
-I took the governor off.

126
00:05:05,650 --> 00:05:06,961
-We have helm, Captain.

127
00:05:06,996 --> 00:05:08,963
-Now entering
Earth's atmosphere.

128
00:05:08,998 --> 00:05:11,000
Hull temperature -- critical.

129
00:05:11,034 --> 00:05:13,416
-Do we have enough power
to escape the atmosphere?

130
00:05:13,451 --> 00:05:16,350
-We won't have control.
We'll be shot into deep space.

131
00:05:16,385 --> 00:05:19,008
I got to have more time.
-We don't have that time.

132
00:05:19,042 --> 00:05:21,321
Get ready to engage
warp engines, Mr. Crow.

133
00:05:21,355 --> 00:05:23,909
-Aye, aye.

134
00:05:23,944 --> 00:05:25,186
-Engage.

135
00:05:25,221 --> 00:05:26,256
[Alarm buzzing]

136
00:05:26,291 --> 00:05:27,913
-Oh, we got movie sign!
-Movie sign!

137
00:05:27,948 --> 00:05:30,157
-I didn't engage
the thing with you.

138
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:45,172
-Look at this,
a Vamuel Goldwyn production.

139
00:05:45,206 --> 00:05:46,380
-Hmm.

140
00:05:46,415 --> 00:05:50,867
-I had an infection
of the yablans one time.

141
00:05:50,902 --> 00:05:53,836
-Ah, the Charlie Daniels Band
is now the Charles Band.

142
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:56,804
-If you ever go down
to the Woolly Swamp...

143
00:05:56,839 --> 00:05:59,048
-Terrible name
for laser-eye surgery,

144
00:05:59,082 --> 00:06:00,532
scares away the customers.

145
00:06:00,567 --> 00:06:03,777
-Come on down to Milford,
free popsicles for the kids.

146
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:07,781
-So what?

147
00:06:07,815 --> 00:06:10,818
They just got people from data
entry to be in this movie?

148
00:06:10,853 --> 00:06:15,616
-Gianni Russo, I remember
her from...maybe not.

149
00:06:15,651 --> 00:06:19,379
-The Keenan Wynn
comes blowing in.

150
00:06:19,413 --> 00:06:22,243
-♪ You are the Wynn
beneath my Keenan ♪

151
00:06:22,278 --> 00:06:24,729
-Oh, isn't he the guy who...
eh.

152
00:06:24,763 --> 00:06:27,317
-No.
-No, he's not.

153
00:06:27,352 --> 00:06:30,804
-♪ Barry Cutler

154
00:06:30,838 --> 00:06:35,878
♪ Ron Masak

155
00:06:35,912 --> 00:06:38,294
-Brother of Bob Mikenko.

156
00:06:41,642 --> 00:06:44,127
-Ah, so you know
it won't be funny.

157
00:06:44,162 --> 00:06:47,890
-Heir to the
Arnold Stang fortune.

158
00:06:47,924 --> 00:06:49,823
-As Dr. Casaba Mellon.

159
00:06:52,066 --> 00:06:54,414
Brother of Neill Stevenko.

160
00:06:54,448 --> 00:06:57,037
-Bro.

161
00:06:57,071 --> 00:07:01,455
-I saw a woolman drinking
a piña colada at Trader Vic's.

162
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:06,460
-Wow, Roddy McDowall 
andDave Allen!

163
00:07:06,495 --> 00:07:08,393
-No reason for them
to tell me all this.

164
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:11,879
I'm no good at names.

165
00:07:11,914 --> 00:07:13,985
-Whoa, is he an American band?

166
00:07:14,019 --> 00:07:17,816
I hope he comes to our town
and helps us party it down.

167
00:07:17,851 --> 00:07:20,923
-These credits give youa chance to finish your popcorn,

168
00:07:20,957 --> 00:07:23,408
talk a little,
decide to see another movie.

169
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:26,376
-The music has a decidedly
Hawkwind feel to it.

170
00:07:26,411 --> 00:07:28,413
-I think it's more like a,
sort of, a Mike Oldfield,

171
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:32,382
McKendree Spring, Rick Wakeman,
Jean-Michel Jarre,

172
00:07:32,417 --> 00:07:34,005
Keith Emerson,
Gentle Giant,

173
00:07:34,039 --> 00:07:37,974
Tomita, Autobahn, Kraftwerk,
Synergy sort of thing.

174
00:07:38,009 --> 00:07:40,080
-I certainly hope we see
those credits

175
00:07:40,114 --> 00:07:41,564
at the end of the movie, too.

176
00:07:41,599 --> 00:07:44,947
-And action.
Cut.

177
00:07:44,981 --> 00:07:46,535
Beautiful.

178
00:07:46,569 --> 00:07:48,709
-These planes were once filled
with wild broccoli like this.

179
00:07:48,744 --> 00:07:50,400
-Hmm.

180
00:07:50,435 --> 00:07:53,645
-"Fievel Goes West."

181
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:57,269
-It looks like Trent Reznor
ran out of gas, poor guy.

182
00:07:57,304 --> 00:07:59,824
-It was after the Acropolis.

183
00:08:03,103 --> 00:08:05,588
-Roxy!

184
00:08:05,623 --> 00:08:11,042
-Somebody, please pull this
garbage disposal off my arm.

185
00:08:11,076 --> 00:08:14,597
-Agh! Robert Smith is in
a good mood today.

186
00:08:14,632 --> 00:08:17,876
-"Edward CD-Player Hand."

187
00:08:17,911 --> 00:08:20,776
-Boy, the Hulk has lost weight.

188
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:22,985
-Remember when he
was over there?

189
00:08:23,019 --> 00:08:25,297
That was a good part
of the movie.

190
00:08:26,954 --> 00:08:28,922
-Man, if I can just get
some butter

191
00:08:28,956 --> 00:08:31,441
to slip in there,
try to slide this thing off.

192
00:08:31,476 --> 00:08:32,926
-Well, back to whatever
I was doing.

193
00:08:35,722 --> 00:08:37,862
-Hmm?

194
00:08:37,896 --> 00:08:41,210
-Norelco's plan
for world domination.

195
00:08:41,244 --> 00:08:44,593
-Even its name spells
Merry Christmas.

196
00:08:44,627 --> 00:08:48,286
-I'm hunting space-cwaft,
ha-ha-ha.

197
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:51,289
-We wish to welcome you
to Denver's Airport.

198
00:08:53,429 --> 00:08:56,466
-Hmm?

199
00:08:56,501 --> 00:08:57,537
-Oh, great.

200
00:08:57,571 --> 00:08:59,815
ET calls, we come,
and he's not here.

201
00:08:59,849 --> 00:09:03,404
-Hey, Yertle, you left
your shell in the ship.

202
00:09:03,439 --> 00:09:04,578
-[Squeaks]

203
00:09:04,613 --> 00:09:07,616
-Hey, hey,
WALL-E, come out here.

204
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:09,514
Help me find Roswell.

205
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:10,584
-[Squeaks]

206
00:09:10,619 --> 00:09:12,690
-Hey, got my shirt
all stretched out.

207
00:09:12,724 --> 00:09:14,761
-[Squeaks]

208
00:09:14,795 --> 00:09:17,557
-I told you to ask directions
at the Gorlon Station

209
00:09:17,591 --> 00:09:18,834
at Zing Ding 5, but no!

210
00:09:18,868 --> 00:09:21,146
You bladzened ahead of that guy
on Bartuo!

211
00:09:21,181 --> 00:09:24,978
-If I could just
pass this football.

212
00:09:25,012 --> 00:09:28,844
-Stop reading my thoughts.
Are you reading my thoughts?

213
00:09:28,878 --> 00:09:32,295
-Look out!
It's Gino Vannelli!

214
00:09:32,330 --> 00:09:35,609
-Tonight, on a very special
"Virginian"...

215
00:09:35,644 --> 00:09:38,232
-Good shooting, Zanthar.
-Thanks, Denise.

216
00:09:41,788 --> 00:09:45,515
-Ah, "Christina's World 3001."

217
00:09:45,550 --> 00:09:47,621
-Help me, Spock.
Spock!

218
00:09:47,656 --> 00:09:49,934
-I know what you're thinking.

219
00:09:49,968 --> 00:09:52,315
Did I fire six gorlocks
or only five?

220
00:09:52,350 --> 00:09:53,869
-Okay, Crow.
That's -- that's enough.

221
00:09:53,903 --> 00:09:56,665
[Whirring]

222
00:09:56,699 --> 00:09:59,322
-[Gasps]
The key to the Amoco bathroom.

223
00:09:59,357 --> 00:10:03,050
-Am I good, huh?
Who's the king? Ha ha ha!

224
00:10:03,085 --> 00:10:04,845
-[Squeaks]

225
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,571
-Look out. ET.

226
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:08,711
[Airplane engine roaring]

227
00:10:08,746 --> 00:10:10,782
-Boy, I love airplanes.
Is that a Cessna?

228
00:10:10,817 --> 00:10:12,370
-No, I think it was Piper.

229
00:10:12,404 --> 00:10:15,200
Ah, let's get out of here.

230
00:10:15,235 --> 00:10:17,720
-Huh, might have used a little
too much buckshot here,

231
00:10:17,755 --> 00:10:19,411
ruined the meat.
[Clicks tongue]

232
00:10:19,446 --> 00:10:22,656
-♪ Closer shave, cleaner shave,
smoother all the way ♪

233
00:10:22,691 --> 00:10:25,728
-Help! A giant bong
is attacking me, oh!

234
00:10:25,763 --> 00:10:27,557
-Mike, this is how I've always
pictured your room.

235
00:10:27,592 --> 00:10:31,182
Am I far off?
-Well...

236
00:10:31,216 --> 00:10:33,529
-Well, off to
weight-loss clinic.

237
00:10:36,670 --> 00:10:38,292
-Get them off me!
Get them off!

238
00:10:38,327 --> 00:10:39,708
Oh, it's just my sheets, hmm.

239
00:10:39,742 --> 00:10:41,813
-Somehow, his mustardy
shorts don't help.

240
00:10:43,815 --> 00:10:46,887
-These are relatively clean,
I guess.

241
00:10:46,922 --> 00:10:50,960
-Ojai.
Crap, I'm still in Ojai.

242
00:10:50,995 --> 00:10:53,687
-Randy Johnson?
Oh, it's her.

243
00:10:53,722 --> 00:10:57,415
-So here's my SlimFast,
Metrecal, Correctol.

244
00:10:57,449 --> 00:10:59,589
-Excuse me, are you my mother?

